<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Quadruped Movement Test</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 20px; }
        .test-section { margin: 20px 0; padding: 15px; border: 1px solid #ccc; }
        .before { background-color: #ffeeee; }
        .after { background-color: #eeffee; }
        code { background-color: #f0f0f0; padding: 2px 4px; border-radius: 3px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>🐎 Quadruped Movement Fix Summary</h1>

    <div class="test-section before">
        <h2>❌ BEFORE (The Problem)</h2>
        <p><strong>Issue:</strong> Quadrupeds could only move in two directions along a fixed ground line.</p>
        <p><strong>Cause:</strong> <code>this.groundLevel = 450</code> forced all feet to Y=450</p>
        <p><strong>Result:</strong> Animals walked only left/right, not freely like the crane</p>
    </div>

    <div class="test-section after">
        <h2>✅ AFTER (The Solution)</h2>
        <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Added adaptive ground level system</p>
        <p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>adaptiveGround: true</code> in creature configs</li>
            <li>Ground level follows mouse target: <code>targetGroundLevel = mouseTarget.y + legLength</code></li>
            <li>Smooth transition: <code>groundLevel += (target - current) * 0.05</code></li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Result:</strong> Quadrupeds now move freely around the entire canvas! 🎉</p>
    </div>

